SUMMARY:IT Gr 12 T1 W1: Pascal 24 SQLite databases in Delphi (or lesson 25\
 , in Lazarus) | What makes a computer fast
DESCRIPTION:CAPS Grade 12 - Pascal - Other four-term independent school (IS
 ASA guideline) - T1 W1\n\nProgramming:\n- Pascal 24 (part): SQLite database
 s in Delphi (or lesson 25\, in Lazarus)\n    focus: SQL from a program\, in
 cluding queries with a parameter from the user\n    https://itcoder.co.za/l
 esson.php?c=pascal&id=capssqlitedelphi\n- Pascal 105 (part): The Grade 12 P
 AT - CAPS\n    focus: starting the PAT: task description and analysis of re
 quirements\n    https://itcoder.co.za/lesson.php?c=pascal&id=capspat12\n\nT
 heory:\n- What makes a computer fast\n    https://itcoder.co.za/lesson.php?
 c=theory12&id=performance\n\nDatabases:\n- SQL 1 (part): Good data in a dat
 abase\n    focus: caring for data: validation\, verification\, integrity\n 
    https://itcoder.co.za/lesson.php?c=sql&id=dbdata\n- SQL 4: A good design
 \n    focus: a good database: integrity\, redundancy\; anomalies\, and remo
 ving them (the concept of normalisation): split tables and create relations
 \n    https://itcoder.co.za/lesson.php?c=sql&id=dbdesign\n- SQL 5: Normalis
 ation step by step\n    focus: anomalies\, and removing them - the concept 
 of normalisation (the formal normal forms go beyond CAPS)\n    https://itco
 der.co.za/lesson.php?c=sql&id=dbnormal
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
